    <DataNode elementId="AT2G36750-MONOMER" textLabel="AT2G36750-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZQ99" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="535" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The UDP glycosyltransferase (UGT) encoded by the &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis UGT73C1&lt;/i&gt; catalyzes the formation of &lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-glucosides. The activity of enzyme was tested on a variety of cytokinins. Two interesting characteristics emerged from that study: i) in contrast to cytokinin-&lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-glycosyltransferases from other species |CITS:[11331778],[12644686]|, recombinant &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt; UGT73C1 catalyzes the glucosylation of both &lt;i&gt;trans&lt;/i&gt;- and &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt;-zeatin |CITS:[15342621]| (albeit with much lesser efficiency that UGT85A1); and ii) unlike UGT85A1, the activity of which was abolished by the 9-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glucosylation of dihydrozeatin, UGT73C1 catalyzes the &lt;i&gt;O&lt;/i&gt;-glucosylation of dihydrozeatin-9-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glc better than other cytokinins, implying that, for this enzyme, glucosylation at one site of the cytokinin improves secondary glucosylations |CITS:[15342621]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G36750-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G36750.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR002213" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Cazy" value="GT1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11926" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9ZQ99" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9ZQ99" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00201" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="Q9ZQ99" />
